1. You have a class that is becoming too large and handling multiple responsibilities. How would you approach refactoring it?

2. You need to add a new feature without modifying existing business logic too much. How would you design it to minimize the impact on existing code?

3. You have multiple implementations of the same functionality, and new implementations may be added later. How would you structure the code?

4. You have a large if-else / switch block based on type or status. How would you improve the design?

5. Two services/classes are tightly coupled, and changes in one frequently break the other. How would you reduce the coupling?

6. A business rule is changing frequently and is scattered across multiple classes. How would you redesign the code so the rule is easier to change?

7. You have duplicate logic across multiple services. How would you decide whether to create a common component or keep the logic separate?

8. A class has too many dependencies injected into it. What would you consider a design smell, and how would you fix it?

9. You need to support different behaviors based on configuration or runtime conditions. How would you design this without continuously adding if-else conditions?

10. You have an existing API used by many clients, but you need to introduce a new behavior without breaking existing consumers. How would you approach it?

11. A service is doing database access, business logic, validation, and external API calls all inside one class. How would you restructure it?

12. You have an operation that can fail and needs retry logic. Where would you put the retry responsibility, and how would you prevent retry logic from being duplicated?

13. Multiple threads can modify the same object/resource simultaneously. How would you identify and solve the concurrency problem?

14. Two requests can update the same database record at the same time. How would you design the application to prevent inconsistent data?

15. You need to add RabbitMQ/Kafka-based asynchronous processing to an existing synchronous flow. How would you change the design?

16. A downstream service is unavailable. Your service currently waits for it and eventually times out. How would you redesign the interaction?

17. You have a workflow with multiple states, such as CREATED → PROCESSING → COMPLETED/FAILED. How would you structure the code so adding new states doesn't make it messy?

18. You have an external provider with a different request/response model from your internal domain model. How would you design the integration so your business logic doesn't depend on the external provider?

19. A feature is becoming difficult to test because the class has many concrete dependencies and external calls. How would you redesign it for testability?

20. A monolithic component needs to be split into multiple microservices. How would you identify boundaries and avoid creating tightly coupled services?
